  "description": "LEJGOY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C49 H50 Cl1 N6 O19 Tb3,H2 O1,C48 H48 Cl1 N6 O19 Tb3. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 5 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.729-3.749 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.95-105.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C97H100Cl2N12O39Tb6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
